  "passage": "Last week, our school organised an expedition to the historic city of York. I was responsible for looking after our group's map and making sure no one got lost. Throughout the day, our teacher, Ms. Clarke, reminded us to stay close and be punctual for meetings. The itinerary included a tour of the York Minster, an amazing cathedral that has stood since the 7th century. For lunch, we enjoyed refreshments at a cosy café, featuring local treats like lemon drizzle cake and fresh sandwiches. Later, we explored the medieval streets under sunny skies, which made the walk even more enjoyable. I heard a talented musician playing the trumpet beautifully there. This trip not only taught me about history but also about being reliable and working as a team. It was an unforgettable adventure!",
